# forge/glass/spec: the glass speculars (envelope r1, FORGE-MATERIAL; PLAN "The envelope" A4 and A7, D53; P2C_CONTRACTS 3d
# "D53's glass"). A STAMP set for the compose glass pass (FORGE-DOLL): KNAPPED's obsidian (metalKind 7) and every GLASS
# alloy (alloyFamilyMetal 5). Absolute metal steps (4 the white-violet hot point, 3 the lit flank): each specular is a hard
# 2-3 px diagonal bar rising to the right with its lit flank under it, so it reads as light lying ON a facet's edge, never
# a 1 px streak (the old pass's 1 px diagonals made the A4 "mask of white streaks"). The pass places ONE stamp per facet of
# 4 px or more (a connected step 1-2 metal plane), its origin on the facet's top-left lit edge, 2-4 a figure, one or more
# off the helm; never inside W7's face box + 1 px nor on a helm's face plate. Pick by the facet's size:
#   bar2    facets 4-8 px    (a 2 px hot bar; group 2 px of step 4)
#   bar3    facets 9-20 px   (a 3 px hot bar on a 2 px flank)
#   kite    facets over 20 px, the torso's and the shield's big planes (a 4-point glint: 3 px hot, a 3 px flank)
#   edge2   a facet whose top-left is its outline corner (a 2 px horizontal hot run on the lit edge; the helm's crown)
# The slide ("Delight: one specular sliding along an obsidian facet as the body turns"): the pass moves the stamp's origin
# along the facet's top edge by the frame's facing and walk phase (D 0, R +1, walk frames +1 on the pass frames), so the
# glint travels as the body turns; it is the same stamp, never a new pixel pattern.
# The rim (D53's second light): `rim` keys, laid by the pass along the 1-2 px inside the step-0 outline at the lower right
# of each convex metal piece of 12 px or more, are runs of step 3 with a step-2 core up-left of them: rimH a bottom edge,
# rimV a right edge, rimC the lower-right corner. The pass may cut a rim to the piece's run (never shorter than 2 px).
# (envelope r3, FORGE-MATERIAL) THE PASS AS BUILT (P2C_CONTRACTS 3d "D53's glass"; FORGE-DOLL owns doll_compose.cpp glassPass,
# the r3 request is MATERIAL/r3/forge_doll_request_r3.patch): planes are runs of steps 2-4 (the drawn step-1 lines part
# the lames); a GLASS alloy's Metal 2 and its armour leather are glass too (obsidian keeps its gold trim and straps); the
# light is a LINE on a plane's top edge out to three fifths of its width (the left edge of a 20 px plane's upper half);
# the inside dark glass; the cold rim 1 px (2 px on a 20 px plane) at the lower right; ONE 2 px diagonal reflection
# band across every plane of 20 px or more; at most 45 % of a plane lit (rim, band, glints kept); 3 speculars a figure.
# These stamps stay the drawn reference for the speculars' shapes (bar2 bar3 kite edge2 rimH rimV rimC).
use person
body adult
role overlay glass.spec
legend 4 metal 4
legend 3 metal 3
legend 2 metal 2
